\DOC X86_SUBROUTINE_SIM_ABBREV_TAC

\TYPE {X86_SUBROUTINE_SIM_ABBREV_TAC : thm * (thm * (thm option array)) * int * thm * thm -> term list -> term -> string -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Symbolically executes a called subroutine in one step by applying a supplied
correctness lemma, advancing the {eventually} goal's state variable to the next
numbered state and abbreviating the subroutine's output as a fresh named
variable.

\DESCRIBE
{X86_SUBROUTINE_SIM_ABBREV_TAC tupper ilist0 comp0 abn n} takes {tupper : thm *
(thm * (thm option array)) * int * thm * thm}, the bundle of the machine-code
definition, the execution/decoding data for that code, a code offset, the code
theorem again, and the correctness theorem for the callee;
{ilist0 : term list}, the terms describing the subroutine's input arguments;
{comp0 : term}, the term describing the output argument location;
{abn : string}, the name given to the fresh variable abbreviating the
subroutine's result; and {n : int}, the index of the state variable to produce
after the call. The conclusion keeps the same {eventually} postcondition, with
its state argument replaced by the state variable of index {n}. Among the
assumptions, all those mentioning the old state — the loaded-code fact, the
register and memory reads, the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation, and the
program-counter/stack-pointer facts — are discarded and re-added as the
corresponding facts about the new state, with the program counter and stack
pointer set to the callee's return values and the {MAYCHANGE} relation extended
by the components the callee may write; purely mathematical assumptions not
mentioning the state are left untouched. Two assumptions are added: a
memory-read fact stating that the output location in the new state holds a
fresh variable named by {abn}, and a conditional arithmetic specification of
that variable derived from the correctness theorem. Writing {A'} for {A} with
the state-dependent assumptions re-indexed and the two new facts about the
abbreviation added:
{
       A ?- eventually ... s_k
    ======================================  X86_SUBROUTINE_SIM_ABBREV_TAC tupper ilist0 comp0 abn n
       A' ?- eventually ... s_n
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, always on
goals whose conclusion is an {eventually} statement about a state reached just
before a subroutine call.

\ENDDOC
